# External integrations

Talk to third parties through a **narrow interface** in our code (`ReferenceProvider`, `PortalPublisher`). Never scatter vendor SDKs across pages.

- Type request and response contracts. Verify webhook signatures; reject stale timestamps.
- Treat provider calls as unreliable: timeouts, retries with backoff, idempotency keys, no infinite loops.
- Record an integration audit: workspace, provider, direction, idempotency key, status, HTTP code, correlation id. Never log ID document images, sensitive evidence, or secrets.
- Locally, use **mocks** behind the same interface. Do not call live AML, portal, or payment APIs unless the owner enables them.
- Do not invent endpoints or assume what a provider accepts. If the real API is unknown, stop and ask.

Background jobs own provider I/O. HTTP handlers enqueue work and return.
